{"body":"For completeness, it’s worth noting that [Pkarr](https://app.pkarr.org/), which [Iroh uses for signed DNS based discovery](https://docs.iroh.computer/concepts/discovery#endpoint-announces-via-pkarr), has a [simple URI scheme](https://github.com/pubky/pkarr/blob/main/design/base.md) that uses z-base32. However, It’s not widely adopted, and the z-base32 is not an IETF standard. \n\nWhile it’s very tempting to adopt, the main problem I see is that this would make it implicit that the a `pk:` uri is an iroh endpoint that serves bytes over iroh-blobs.\n\nBy going with `radiroh://` we maintain full control and resonsibility over specifying what this URL scheme means, spanning both peer discovery details  (resolving a key to an iroh relay/IP address), and transfer protocol (iroh-blobs).","embeds":[],"id":"80aae2ae5dec00de67fd1567217e3ed90a5cac62","type":"comment.edit"}